    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i need some advice for a cow that just had a rumenotomy done earlier today. whats the best way to monitor the incision for infection and when can i start putting her back on solid feed? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the rumenotomy, you need to monitor the incision for signs of infection, which can include excessive redness, swelling, pus discharge, or foul odor around the surgical site. Keep a close eye on her general demeanor, too; lethargy or fever are also red flags. You should consult with your veterinarian regarding the exact timeline for reintroducing solid feed, as this depends on the complexity of the surgery and your cow's recovery rate. It's crucial to follow their specific post-operative instructions for feeding.",
